# Files that start a process themselves (tools/check-process-starts.py, a copy of appkit's; docs/PROCESSES.md):
# <path> <count of lines found> <reason>
# streamtap is not built on appkit; its two helpers are the named exception of the plan "no visible shell and
# background processes" (the sink, ffmpeg and ffprobe), each child without a console window and bound to the window.

# The window starts the sink (serve, mux): CREATE_NO_WINDOW, put into a job with KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE (jobs::KillOnClose).
desktop/crates/streamtap-app/src/sink.rs 2 the window's helper for the sink (no window, bound to the window by its job)
# The sink starts ffmpeg and ffprobe: an argv, CREATE_NO_WINDOW, a time limit.
desktop/crates/streamtap-sink/src/proc.rs 2 the sink's helper for ffmpeg and ffprobe (no window, a time limit)

# Tests only: the module is #[cfg(all(test, windows))], which the check does not take for a test module.
desktop/crates/streamtap-app/src/jobs.rs 4 the tests of the job (a child that outlives its owner, ended by the job)
